<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"> <head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><meta name="description" content="reachq is graph infrastructure for reachability and shortest paths on dense directed graphs."><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/reachq/favicon.svg"><title>reachq — Graph infrastructure, queryable</title></head> <body> <header class="site-header"><div class="shell nav-wrap"> <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="reachq home"><img class="brand-lockup" src="/reachq/logo-reversed.svg" alt="reachq" /></a> <button class="menu-toggle" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-expanded="false">Menu</button> <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#why">Why reachq</a><a href="#product">What it does</a><a href="#workflow">How it works</a><a href="#api">API</a><a href="#research">Research</a><a href="#docs">Docs</a></nav> <div class="nav-actions"><a class="nav-github" href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a><a class="button button-small" href="#install">Get started <span>→</span></a></div> </div></header> <main id="top"> <section class="hero shell"><div class="hero-copy"> <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Graph infrastructure for Python</div> <h1>Make dense graphs<br><em>feel small.</em></h1> <p class="hero-lede">reachq turns hard reachability and shortest-path problems into fast, testable building blocks for the systems and research teams pushing graph algorithms forward.</p> <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#install">Start building <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the source <span>↗</span></a></div> <div class="trust-row"><span>MIT licensed</span><span>Python 3.10+</span><span>Deterministic by default</span></div> </div> <div class="hero-visual"><div class="visual-glow"></div><div class="visual-topline"><span>REACHQ / LIVE GRAPH</span><span class="live"><i></i> ready</span></div> <svg class="graph-art" viewBox="0 0 560 460" role="img" aria-label="Graph nodes connected by query paths"><defs><linearGradient id="line" x1="0" x2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#4d5b6e" stop-opacity=".2"></stop><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#b8ff65"></stop><stop offset="1" stop-color="#69e0ff" stop-opacity=".45"></stop></linearGradient></defs><g class="graph-lines"><path d="M54 322 L144 150 L248 260 L340 106 L458 190 L520 80"></path><path d="M54 322 L184 382 L248 260 L366 356 L458 190"></path><path d="M144 150 L340 106 L366 356"></path><path d="M248 260 L458 190 L520 80"></path><path d="M184 382 L366 356 L520 80"></path></g><path class="query-line" d="M54 322 L144 150 L248 260 L340 106 L458 190 L520 80"></path><g class="graph-nodes"><circle cx="54" cy="322" r="10"></circle><circle cx="144" cy="150" r="7"></circle><circle cx="184" cy="382" r="7"></circle><circle cx="248" cy="260" r="12"></circle><circle cx="340" cy="106" r="8"></circle><circle cx="366" cy="356" r="8"></circle><circle cx="458" cy="190" r="11"></circle><circle cx="520" cy="80" r="8"></circle></g><circle class="pulse" cx="248" cy="260" r="21"></circle><circle class="pulse pulse-delay" cx="458" cy="190" r="19"></circle></svg> <div class="visual-footer"><span>2,048 vertices</span><span>•</span><span>12,816 edges</span><span class="visual-bound">bound <strong>O(log n)</strong></span></div></div></section> <section class="section why-section" id="why"><div class="shell why-grid"><div class="why-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Why graph queries get hard</div><h2>The graph is the data.<br><span>The search is the cost.</span></h2><p>In a dense directed graph, one reachability question can fan out across a huge portion of the graph. A shortest-path query adds weights, repeated relaxations, and a decision about how much approximation is acceptable.</p></div><div class="why-list"><article><span class="why-number">01</span><div><h3>Naive traversal repeats work</h3><p>Running BFS or Dijkstra from scratch is simple, but expensive when many sources ask related questions.</p></div></article><article><span class="why-number">02</span><div><h3>Precompute the useful edges</h3><p>reachq adds carefully chosen shortcuts so later queries can skip redundant exploration while preserving the property you care about.</p></div></article><article><span class="why-number">03</span><div><h3>Keep the reasoning inspectable</h3><p>Seeds, refinement flags, bounds, and invariants stay explicit. You can profile a result without treating the algorithm as a black box.</p></div></article></div></div></section> <section class="section section-border" id="product"><div class="shell"><div class="section-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">One engine. Three outcomes.</div><h2>From graph complexity<br><span>to useful signal.</span></h2></div><p>Built for engineers who need production-shaped primitives and researchers who need the math to stay visible.</p></div> <div class="pillars"><article class="pillar"><span>01</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Construct shortcut sets and hopsets that make dense directed graphs easier to query.</p><a href="#api">Explore build <span>→</span></a></article><article class="pillar"><span>02</span><h3>Accelerate</h3><p>Run reachability and shortest-path queries with optional process-level parallelism.</p><a href="#api">Explore accelerate <span>→</span></a></article><article class="pillar"><span>03</span><h3>Verify</h3><p>Keep invariants, bounds, and deterministic seeds close to every experiment.</p><a href="#api">Explore verify <span>→</span></a></article></div></div></section> <section class="section feature-section"><div class="shell feature-grid"><div class="feature-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Designed around the query</div><h2>Keep the graph.<br><span>Lose the drag.</span></h2><p>Shortcut sets and hopsets add just enough structure to make the next question cheaper—without hiding how the answer was derived.</p><a class="text-link" href="#workflow">See the workflow <span>→</span></a></div><div class="feature-stack"><article class="surface-card"><div class="surface-icon">↗</div><div><div class="surface-label">Reachability</div><h3>Know what can reach what.</h3><p>Preserve exact reachability while reducing the work your queries need to do.</p></div><span class="surface-arrow">↗</span></article><article class="surface-card surface-card-active"><div class="surface-icon">⌁</div><div><div class="surface-label">Shortest paths</div><h3>Bound the hops, not the truth.</h3><p>Use weighted hopsets for fast approximate SSSP with an explicit error budget.</p></div><span class="surface-arrow">↗</span></article><article class="surface-card"><div class="surface-icon">✦</div><div><div class="surface-label">Research-grade</div><h3>Make every run repeatable.</h3><p>Deterministic construction, configurable refinements, and citation-ready outputs.</p></div><span class="surface-arrow">↗</span></article></div></div></section> <section class="section architecture-section"><div class="shell"><div class="architecture-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">What reachq actually builds</div><h2>Two constructions.<br><span>Two kinds of leverage.</span></h2></div><p>The right structure depends on the question. reachq keeps the distinction clear so your implementation can stay clear too.</p></div><div class="architecture-grid"><article class="architecture-card"><div class="architecture-tag">For exact reachability</div><h3>Shortcut sets</h3><p>A shortcut set augments the original directed graph with additional edges. Queries can traverse the augmented graph, while the library checks that reachability is preserved.</p><div class="architecture-flow"><span>G</span><b>+</b><span>H<sub>shortcuts</sub></span><b>→</b><strong>same reachability</strong></div><a href="#api">See the reachability API <span>→</span></a></article><article class="architecture-card architecture-card-accent"><div class="architecture-tag">For weighted SSSP</div><h3>Hopsets</h3><p>A hopset adds weighted links that reduce the number of hops in a path. You choose an epsilon, then compare the bounded result with the exact baseline.</p><div class="architecture-flow"><span>G</span><b>+</b><span>H<sub>weighted</sub></span><b>→</b><strong>(1 + ε) distance</strong></div><a href="#api">See the hopset API <span>→</span></a></article></div></div></section> <section class="section how-section"><div class="shell how-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">How a query gets answered</div><h2>Separate the expensive<br><span>setup from the question.</span></h2><p class="how-lede">The first run pays for construction. Every query after that gets a reusable structure instead of starting from zero.</p></div><div class="how-steps"><div><span>1</span><h3>Construct once</h3><p>Build a shortcut set or hopset with a fixed seed and configuration. The returned beta and bound describe the realized construction.</p></div><div><span>2</span><h3>Query many times</h3><p>Run BFS, parallel BFS, Dijkstra, or hop-bounded shortest paths against the original graph plus its augmentation.</p></div><div><span>3</span><h3>Check the invariant</h3><p>Use reachability-preservation checks or compare approximate distances against an exact baseline in your tests.</p></div></div></div></section> <section class="section guarantees-section"><div class="shell"><div class="guarantees-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Know the contract</div><h2>Useful because the<br><span>tradeoffs are visible.</span></h2></div><p>reachq is an algorithmic toolkit, not a hosted graph database. It gives you primitives, checks, and knobs—not a magic black box.</p></div><div class="guarantees-grid"><article><span class="guarantee-icon">✓</span><h3>Preserves reachability</h3><p>For shortcut-set workflows, the invariant is exact: adding shortcuts should not change which vertices are reachable.</p></article><article><span class="guarantee-icon">≈</span><h3>Bounds approximation</h3><p>For hopsets, epsilon is explicit. You can make the accuracy/performance tradeoff part of the call site and test suite.</p></article><article><span class="guarantee-icon">↺</span><h3>Reproduces runs</h3><p>Use a random seed and refinement configuration to make experiments comparable across machines and iterations.</p></article><article><span class="guarantee-icon">!</span><h3>Shows its limits</h3><p>The project is research software. Read the limitations and benchmarks before treating a construction as production infrastructure.</p></article></div></div></section> <section class="section workflow-section" id="workflow"><div class="shell"><div class="workflow-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">A compact mental model</div><h2>One path from <em>raw</em><br>to <span>reliable.</span></h2></div><p>Compose the parts you need. Leave the rest out of the hot path.</p></div><div class="workflow-rail"><div class="rail-line"></div><div class="workflow-step"><div class="step-index">01</div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-kicker">Input</div><h3>A directed graph</h3><p>Start with your graph as-is. Weighted or unweighted, dense or sparse.</p></div></div><div class="workflow-step"><div class="step-index">02</div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-kicker">Construction</div><h3>A smaller search space</h3><p>Build shortcuts, tune refinements, and keep the construction deterministic.</p></div></div><div class="workflow-step"><div class="step-index">03</div><div class="step-card"><div class="step-kicker">Result</div><h3>A query you can trust</h3><p>Check exact reachability or bounded shortest-path results against clear invariants.</p></div></div></div></div></section> <section class="section code-section" id="api"><div class="shell code-grid"><div class="code-copy"><div class="eyebrow">A focused Python API</div><h2>Readable enough<br>to <span>research.</span></h2><p>No query language to learn. Import the construction you need, keep your parameters explicit, and build from there.</p><div class="code-tabs"><button class="code-tab active" data-tab="reachability">Reachability</button><button class="code-tab" data-tab="hopset">Hopset</button></div></div><div class="code-window"><div class="code-bar"><span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>example.py</span><span class="copy-label">copy</span></div><pre id="code-reachability"><code><span class="code-purple">from</span> reachq.shortcut <span class="code-purple">import</span> build_shortcut_set_for_reachability

shortcuts, beta, bound = build_shortcut_set_for_reachability(
  graph, omega=<span class="code-green">3.0</span>, random_seed=<span class="code-green">42</span>
)</code></pre><pre id="code-hopset" hidden><code><span class="code-purple">from</span> reachq.hopset <span class="code-purple">import</span> build_hopset_for_sssp

hopset, beta = build_hopset_for_sssp(
  graph, epsilon=<span class="code-green">0.1</span>, random_seed=<span class="code-green">42</span>
)

<span class="code-comment"># (1 + epsilon)-approximate SSSP</span></code></pre><div class="code-status"><span><i></i> deterministic run</span><span>Python · reachq 0.9</span></div></div></div></section> <section class="section docs-section" id="docs"><div class="shell"><div class="docs-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Documentation that answers the next question</div><h2>Start with the concept.<br><span>Then open the implementation.</span></h2></div><p>Each page has a job: get a first construction running, explain the algorithm, show the public surface, or make the limits explicit.</p></div><div class="docs-grid"><a href="https://sachncs.github.io/reachq/getting-started.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">01</span><h3>Quick start</h3><p>Install from source and build your first shortcut set in a few minutes.</p><span class="doc-link">First construction →</span></a><a href="https://sachncs.github.io/reachq/reference.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">02</span><h3>API reference</h3><p>Find every public function, signature, configuration option, and return value.</p><span class="doc-link">Browse the API →</span></a><a href="https://sachncs.github.io/reachq/algorithms.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">03</span><h3>Algorithms</h3><p>Understand JLS shortcut sets, CFR hopsets, refinements, and the bound each path targets.</p><span class="doc-link">Read the model →</span></a><a href="https://sachncs.github.io/reachq/examples.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">04</span><h3>Examples</h3><p>See the library used for RAG reranking, GNN preprocessing, compiler graphs, and more.</p><span class="doc-link">See applications →</span></a><a href="https://sachncs.github.io/reachq/benchmarks.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">05</span><h3>Benchmarks</h3><p>Compare construction sizes, query behavior, and the work behind the claims.</p><span class="doc-link">Inspect results →</span></a><a href="https://sachncs.github.io/reachq/limitations.html" class="doc-card"><span class="doc-index">06</span><h3>Limitations</h3><p>Know what is experimental, what is not implemented, and when to use NetworkX or igraph instead.</p><span class="doc-link">Read before shipping →</span></a></div></div></section><section class="section research-section" id="research"><div class="shell research-panel"><div class="research-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Built from the paper</div><h2>Research-grade<br><span>by design.</span></h2><p>The constructions follow <em>Parallel Reachability and Shortest Paths on Non-sparse Digraphs</em> by Ashvinkumar, Bernstein, Probst Gutenberg, and Saranurak.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View on GitHub <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="research-stats"><div><strong>100%</strong><span>pure Python core</span></div><div><strong>0.1</strong><span>example epsilon</span></div><div><strong>∞</strong><span>graphs to explore</span></div></div></div></section> <section class="section install-section" id="install"><div class="shell install-panel"><div><div class="eyebrow">Ready when you are</div><h2>Give your graph<br><em>some leverage.</em></h2></div><div><div class="install-command"><span>$</span> pip install -e ".[dev]" <button aria-label="Copy install command">⧉</button></div><p>Clone the repo, run the examples, and start asking better questions of your graph.</p><a class="text-link light-link" href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the quick start <span>→</span></a></div></div></section> </main> <footer class="footer"><div class="shell footer-wrap"><a class="brand" href="#top"><img class="brand-lockup" src="/reachq/logo-reversed.svg" alt="reachq" /></a><span>Graph reachability, queryable.</span><div><a href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/sachncs/reachq/blob/master/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MIT License</a></div></div></footer> <script type="module">const c=document.querySelector(".menu-toggle"),n=document.querySelector(".nav-links");c?.addEventListener("click",()=>{const e=n?.classList.toggle("nav-open");c.setAttribute("aria-expanded",String(e))});document.querySelectorAll(".code-tab").forEach(e=>e.addEventListener("click",()=>{document.querySelectorAll(".code-tab").forEach(t=>t.classList.remove("active")),e.classList.add("active"),document.querySelectorAll(".code-window pre").forEach(t=>t.hidden=t.id!=="code-"+e.dataset.tab)}));document.querySelector('[aria-label="Copy install command"]')?.addEventListener("click",async e=>{await navigator.clipboard?.writeText('pip install -e ".[dev]"'),e.currentTarget.textContent="✓"});</script> </body></html>
